mech_psi first, then the source position is a confirmation, not a prerequisite.{"at":1786996721628,"body":"Decomposition just opened:\n\nWhat would suffice:\nWhat the run says would suffice:\nThe ledger entry is correct. The `pe1006-psi` goals entry now reflects the true state of the run. My deliverable — the skeleton file — is written and the derived ledger carries the corrected statuses.\n\n## Report\n\n**Slug:** `research/backward/pe1006-psi.md`\n\nI rewrote the existing skeleton to reflect what the run *actually holds*, which had drifted from the file. The decomposition itself was sound; the statuses were stale in four places.\n\n**The decomposition** (unchanged in structure — it was right):\n\n- **G1** fixes the index set: the k+1 length-k Fibonacci subwords = the length-k factors of the infinite Fibonacci word F, Sturmian of slope 1/φ², so Ψ(k) is a sum over m = 0..k.\n- **G2** turns each factor into a decimal v(xₘ) via the mechanical-word digit rule, corrected slope F(n−2)/F(n).\n- **G3** telescopes v into a geometrically weighted floor sum, so Ψ(k) is its second moment.\n- **G4** evaluates that second moment in O(log k) by the universal-Euclidean monoid — the step that reaches 10^18.\n\nThe `implies` field states the actual left-to-right inference: each lemma supplies the index-set/term/telescoped-form/evaluation the next consumes, with no quantifier gaps.\n\n**Gaps left open:**\n\n- **G1** — infinite-limit stabilisation of the finite nested factor chain into the limit word (the Lean `fib_subword_count` is still a sorry). Not the critical path.\n- **G4** — the *wiring*: the primitive `code/lib/ueuclid.py` is built and its O(log) correctness is discharged on the library's word, but no in-container captured file yet reproduces the anchors 34432237/20938836 *through the monoid*, and 10^18 has not been run under two approximants. This is the critical path.\n\n**Discharged since the old skeleton** (this is the cheap result — marking them discharged rather than re