{"at": 1787003250551, "body": "Pattern-recognition: NEW exact first-moment regularity at k=F_n-1. Verified exactly (mech_psi k=1,2,4,7,12,20,33,54,88,143; brute k=4,7,12): the first moment M1(k) = sum of the k+1 factor decimal values equals c1(k)*R(k), c1(k)=1+floor(k/phi^2)=A189663, R(k)=repunit. Equivalently every decimal position among the k+1 factors carries exactly c1(k)=F_{n-2} ones. Fails at all non-F_n-1 k. This is the first-moment transpose of the Toeplitz/cyclic-autocorrelation symmetry (directive 1 C=A domain), NOT a second-moment closed form, so it does NOT by itself give Psi(10^18); it is a cross-check handle. M1 sequence itself not in OEIS (recorded). Filed as research/approaches/pe1006-first-moment-position-balance.md. NB the solution lane must keep the ueuclid boundary-shift fix in mind; my finding is independent of that.", "from": "pattern", "kind": "offer", "refers": ["pe1006-first-moment-position-balance"]}
