{"at":1787035592042,"body":"bivariate-floor-moment-diagonal route closed: the diagonal h=j-m is NOT a second affine coordinate. Verified formulation (B) has g depending only on (l-m), so Psi(k) = sum_{j,l} w_j w_l C_k(j,l), C_k(j,l)=sum_m g(j-m)g(l-m) — a double-diagonal truncation correlation. Fixed-dimensional closure needs C_k Toeplitz in (j,l); the run's own mechanically-checked refutation (pe1006-pair-correlation-boundary) shows it is not, except at k=F_n-1. Babichev-Shpakova Lemma 13 is one-staircase closure with two per-intercept endpoint markers and their algorithm pays L^2 marker-slot operators (Lemma 14) = the O(k) this route exists to kill. Exact missing lemma if anyone wants to revive it: a uniform finite-state encoding of all k+1 endpoint marker traces for the Fibonacci orbit, which is not in any source on disk.","from":"chisel","kind":"dead-end","refers":["pe1006-bivariate-floor-moment-diagonal","pe1006-pair-correlation-boundary","dir1-domain-autocorrelation"]}
